    "content": "The inaugural Fleet Week Houston takes place April 15–22, 2026, marking the first time a Texas city has hosted this U.S. Navy event. Featuring ships like the USS Kearsarge, the weeklong event offers free public ship tours, a parade of ships, and community events to honor over 1,000 Sailors, Marines, and Coast Guardsmen.Key Details and Events:Location: Port of Houston and Seawolf Park.Ship Tours: Free to the public, first-come-first-served, with a queue system.Ship Tour Rules: Closed-toed shoes required, no large bags/backpacks, no strollers, and visitors must be able to navigate steep ladders.Events: A parade of ships occurred April 15, with community events including a drone show, aviation exhibits, and brewery events spanning the week.Vessels: Includes the USS Kearsarge (LHD-3), USS Minneapolis-St. Paul (LCS-21), USS St. Louis (LCS-19), and USCGC Edgar Culbertson.For the most up-to-date schedule and potential, visit fleetweekhouston.com. The inaugural Fleet Week Houston takes place April 15–22, 2026, marking the first time a Texas city has hosted this U.S. Navy event. Featuring ships like the USS Kearsarge, the weeklong event offers free public ship tours, a parade of ships, and community events to honor over 1,000 Sailors, Marines, and Coast Guardsmen. Key Details and Events: Location: Port of Houston and Seawolf Park. Ship Tours: Free to the public, first-come-first-served, with a queue system. Ship Tour Rules: Closed-toed shoes required, no large bags/backpacks, no strollers, and visitors must be able to navigate steep ladders. Events: A parade of ships occurred April 15, with community events including a drone show, aviation exhibits, and brewery events spanning the week. Vessels: Includes the USS Kearsarge (LHD-3), USS Minneapolis-St. Paul (LCS-21), USS St. Louis (LCS-19), and USCGC Edgar Culbertson. For the most up-to-date schedule and potential, visit fleetweekhouston.com. fleetweekhouston.com",
